-- title:
--   Maximal ideal at the cusp ∞ generated by p and 1/j
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $M \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ (no coprimality between $p$ and $M$ is assumed). Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M` be the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $j(\mathfrak q^{d})$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid M$. Let $B =$ `chartAlgInf M p` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[u]$, where $u = j^{-1}$ is the element `jInvChartInf M p` of $B$. The assertion is: for every $b \in B$ whose $\mathfrak q$-expansion has coefficient of index $0$ of the form $p\,c$ with $c \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, there exist $s, c, d \in B$ such that the coefficient of index $0$ of the expansion of $s$ is *not* of the form $p\,c'$ with $c' \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, and $s\,b = p\,c + u\,d$ holds in $B$.
--
--   The prime $\mathfrak m \subseteq B$ of elements whose constant $\mathfrak q$-coefficient lies in $p\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ is the reduction modulo $p$ of the cusp $\infty$ on the pole chart of the two-chart model of $X_0(M)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$; the statement says that after localising at $\mathfrak m$ the maximal ideal is generated by $p$ and $u = 1/j$, so that the chart is unramified over the $u$-line there with trivial residue extension. It is used, together with finiteness of $B$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[u]$, by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty) and [`ModularCurve.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_cuspInfty`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_cuspInfty) to get regularity of the local ring at the cusp $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_exists_mul_eq_natCast_mul_add_jInvChartInf_mul_of_coeff_zero_mem.lean

